### Mission workflow

Use the `standard` pipeline for features and multi-file changes. Use `quick` for single-module bugfixes. Use `coverage` for test gaps.

```bash
# Scaffold a mission from conversation context
/mission

# Create and dispatch
ethos mission create --file .tmp/missions/<name>.yaml
Agent(subagent_type=<worker>, run_in_background=true)
# Worker reads: ethos mission show <id>

# Track
ethos mission show <id>
ethos mission log <id>
ethos mission results <id>

# Close
ethos mission close <id>                              # pass
ethos mission reflect <id> --file <path>              # needs another round
ethos mission advance <id>
ethos mission close <id> --status failed              # fail
```

Review-cycle fix rounds (Copilot/Bugbot findings) use bare `Agent()`, not missions — these are mechanical fixes where the write-set is obvious.
